  "sample": {
    "description": "Panel of 11 EU-acceding CEE countries (Bulgaria, Czechia, Estonia, Croatia, Latvia, Lithuania, Hungary, Poland, Romania, Slovenia, Slovakia) observed annually 1995-2024. Regressor matrix x: 11x29 (1995-2023) x7 factors (X1 GDPpc PPS EU27=100, X2 price level, X3 cum FDI %GDP, X4 trade %GDP, X5 cum GCF %GDP, X6 gov debt %GDP (S13 proxy), X7 private debt). Dependent delta_y: 11x29 annual changes 1996-2024. Total pooled NT=319.",
    "n": 319,
    "start": "1995-01-01",
    "end": "2024-12-31",
    "same_as_paper": true,
    "missing": 0,
    "extra": 0,
    "differences": "",
    "cannot_count": "",
    "not_rebuilt": {},
    "substitutions": "Eurostat prc_ppp_ind EU27_2020 for X1 (VI_PPS_EU27_2020_HAB GDP) and X2 (PLI_EU27_2020 GDP); ESTAT gov_10dd_edpt1 S13 general government debt used as proxy for X6 central government debt due to missing S1311 history for 5 countries (BG,CZ,EE,LV,SK pre-2022) in current ESTAT vintage; World Bank WDI BX.KLT.DINV.WD.GD.ZS, NE.TRD.GNFS.ZS, NE.GDI.TOTL.ZS for X3/X4/X5 with X3/X5 accumulated as cumulative sum from 1995 inclusive; Eurostat tipspd20 (S11_S14_S15 consolidated, PC_GDP) for X7. Standardization pooled NT=n_pooled_computed, Omega eigendecomposition, orthogonal preconditioner, yearly OLS N=11 per t, delta-method SEs as in paper. Data vintage July 2026 may include post-publication revisions (notably BG 1996 gov debt outlier 244.5% and Slovakia FDI revisions) causing small mean/corr deviations."
  },
  "notes": "Eurostat API choice: prc_ppp_ind dataset, freq A, ppp_cat GDP, na_item VI_PPS_EU27_2020_HAB for X1 and PLI_EU27_2020 for X2, geo BG etc, time 1995-2024. Eurostat tipspd20 for X7 private debt consolidated S11_S14_S15 F3_F4 PC_GDP. Gov debt: paper specifies central S1311 GD PC_GDP from gov_10dd_edpt1, but current API returns only 4 years (2022-2025) for BG/CZ/EE/LV/SK, implying 152 missing pooled obs if used; we substitute S13 general government debt (GD) which yields complete obs and country means within 1-2 pts of paper, median identical 37.4. BG 1996 outlier 244.5% remains in S13 series, raising pooled SD/kurt vs paper max 99; capping not applied to keep raw public vintage.\n\nWorld Bank WDI: FDI net inflows %GDP, trade %GDP, GCF %GDP fetched 1995-2024. Accumulation: X3 and X5 cumulative sum inclusive from 1995 (X_{1995}= flow_{1995}, X_t = sum_{1995}^{t} flow), matching Table country means for window 1995-2023 (paper note says 1996-2024 but numbers match 1995-2023). Trade X4 used as level (not accumulated).\n\nStandardization: mu_j = mean over pooled sample, sigma_j = sample SD ddof1, z = (x-mu)/sigma, Omega = cor(z). Eigendecomposition with descending eigenvalues, W orthogonal, P = Z W, cov(P)=Lambda.\n\nRegression: For each t 1996-2024, cross-section N=11, regress delta_y on 1+P_{t-1}, d=7, df=3. Back-transform beta = diag(sigma)^{-1} W gamma, alpha = alpha^P - mu beta. SEs via delta method M cov M^T (M as in paper). R2, adjR2=1-(1-R2)(n-1)/(n-d-1), Residual SD = sqrt(mse_resid), F.\n\nDecomposition: delta_y_{j}=alpha_t/d + beta_{t-1,j} x_{t-1,j}, kappa_{t,j}=GDP1995/d + sum delta_j, Total= sum kappa, err^a = sum resid = GDP Regr - GDP Data. Lambda(t) relative debt not needed for headline claims.\n\nDeviations: Pooled X3 mean 78.41 vs paper 77.06, X6 mean 38.76 vs 38.37, corr X1-X6 0.172 vs 0.220 etc due to BG outlier and latest WDI revisions (SK FDI). Residual pooled SD 0.779 vs 0.747, JB p <0.001 vs 0.017 due to same outlier, Bartlett B 186 vs 193. Kappa components within ~10 PPS of Table1 (e.g., BG X2 129 vs 143, EE X7 -82 vs -93) directionally same, Baltic divergence preserved (LT -33 vs EE -82). Choices paper leaves open: no risk-free rate, standard calendar year, EU27_2020 base."
